  "display_number": "S23",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S23. Attrition sensitivity analyses.",
  "panel": "A",
  "panel_title": "Panel a. Baseline (2011) characteristics of participants retained in the analytical cohort versus 2011-only participants.",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Values are mean (SD) or n (%) on an available-data basis (per-variable N: 2,785–3,197 retained; 1,518–1,757 2011-only). Standardised differences are the mean difference divided by the pooled SD (continuous) or the proportion difference divided by sqrt(p(1−p)) (binary). The recalibrated PhenoAge scale (correlation ~0.68 with the primary-analysis BAA) was used because the primary BAA derivation cannot be reproduced for participants outside the analytical sample from the delivered code. BMI summaries exclude values outside the plausible range of 12-60 kg m⁻²."
  ],
